server.py<pre><code>from fastmcp import FastMCP

mcp = FastMCP("echo-server", version="2025-03-26")

@mcp.tool(description="Echo text back with optional casing tweaks")
def echo(text: str, upper: bool = False) -&gt; str:
    """Return the submitted text."""
    return text.upper() if upper else text

@mcp.tool
def word_count(text: str) -&gt; int:
    """Count characters separated by whitespace."""
    return len(text.split())

if __name__ == "__main__":
    mcp.run()  # defaults to stdio transport for local clients
</code></pre> <p>Key FastMCP features at play:</p> <ul> <li><code>FastMCP(name, version)</code> registers metadata the Gateway will surface.</li> <li><code>@mcp.tool</code> pulls argument schemas from Python type hints and docstrings.</li> <li><code>mcp.run()</code> picks STDIO by default; pass <code>transport="http"</code> for Streamable HTTP.</li> </ul>
